    "introduction": "Hi! I'm Guo Zijian, but you can also call me Melon. I'm currently an undergraduate student at School of Physics, Peking University, and I expect to graduate in 2029. My current academic interests lie in biophysics, particularly the fascinating phenomena associated with epigenetics.\n\nBut there's much more to me than physics! I enjoy a wide variety of hobbies, including playing the piano, volleyball, and softball, drawing, and roller skating. I've been an active member of PKUCC, the roller skating club at my university, for quite a while, so don't be surprised if I end up talking about roller skating quite a lot!\n\nThrough this page, I hope to share a vibrant and multifaceted side of myself — not just as a physics student, but as someone with diverse passions and interests.\n\nAbove all, I want to share my love for this wonderful world and all the little things that make it special.\n\nIt's lovely to meet you. Happy to be your friend! :)",
